Description: fate/hevc: cover deferred multilayer access unit boundaries
 Insert a layer-six prefix SEI before an access unit and a repeated PPS
 between the two pictures of another access unit. Check packet sizes
 and checksums, and compare both decoded views with the existing
 mv_nuh_layer_id.bit reference. No coded picture changes.
 .
 Add a longer prefix variant and feed it one byte at a time to exercise
 a buffered boundary whose offset equals END_NOT_FOUND. An API test
 also checks packet positions and timestamps when the prefix spans
 more input buffers than the parser timestamp history can retain.
 Keep the expected output in tests/ref/fate.
 .
 Generate both samples with make-hevc-au-boundaries.py from the
 accompanying sample request. Install mv-au-boundaries.hevc and
 mv-au-boundaries-buffered.hevc in the FATE suite's hevc directory.
 .
 Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
 Assisted-by: Claude Opus via Claude Code
 Assisted-by: GPT-6 via Codex
 .
